    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/marketing-specialist-main-campus-administration-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states-ede80221-190c-47ff-87a4-a0a859c7fa0c": {
      "title": "Marketing Specialist - Main Campus",
      "description": "Marketing Specialist - Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Marketing Specialist - Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Marketing Specialist 501698 Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH Administration Administrative Support Full-Time Marketing/Communication None Show More Show Less Staff - Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Marketing Specialist Department Org: University Marketing - 104840 Employee Classification: U1 - Unclassified PSA FT Bargaining Unit: Professional Staff Association Primary Location: MC AD Shift: 1 Start Time: 8:15 am End Time: 5:00 pm Posted Salary: Starting at $49,900 Float: no Rotate: no On Call: no Travel: no Weekend/Holiday: no Job Description: This in-person role serves as lead marketing representative for the College of Health and Human Services to provide reliable counsel, develop and execute marketing campaigns that support achievement of the college’s business objectives and build strong, lasting relationships. This position must understand the college’s needs and objectives and ensure marketing tactics and strategies align with University standards and priorities. Job Summary: Join the University of Toledo’s College of Natural Sciences and Mathematics and help bring the power of discovery to life. You’ll work alongside research-engaged faculty and students, sharing stories that showcase nationally recognized programs in physics and astronomy, photovoltaics and materials science. From groundbreaking research to community outreach that makes science accessible and engaging for all, you’ll help communicate the discoveries, people and ideas shaping our understanding of the world. If you’re a creative storyteller who enjoys helping connect students with their passion for science and data, making complex topics compelling and connecting audiences with the impact of discovery, this is an opportunity to make a meaningful difference. Minimum Qualifications: Education/Experience/Licensure: • Bachelor’s degree in communications, public relations, marketing, business or other closely related fields is required. • Prefer minimum of two (2) years of marketing and/or project management experience. • Excellent computer skills in Microsoft Office -- strong Excel, Power Point and Word skills and Marketing Specialist experience is required. Communication and other skills: • Excellent written (including editing) and oral communication skills. • Knowledge of or ability to learn and adhere to AP Style guidelines. • Self-motivated with the ability to follow directions while working independently. • High proficiency in project management, attention to detail, prioritization of work and organizational skills required. • Ability to build relationships and develop trust with stakeholders. • Ability to contribute to team projects. • A high degree of professionalism and strong work ethic coupled with a sense of responsibility and integrity required. • Ability to work under minimal supervision, tight time constraints, and periodic high-volume circumstances. • Willingness and ability to take direction from various sources required. • Must be flexible and available outside of normal business hours. May be required to respond to urgent matters at all times of the day and/or on scheduled days off. Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements for the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center will include drug and other required health screenings for the position. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to attracting and retaining the best and brightest talent and fostering a culture of respect. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact HR Compliance at hrcompliance@utoledo.edu or 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m. or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the Center for Administrative Support on the UToledo Main Campus. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) ed9381b9 Last Name (required) e61816db Email (required) a081e21f Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 738b6608 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from