    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/program-manager-student-engagement-main-campus-student-affairs-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states": {
      "title": "Program Manager Student Engagement - Main Campus",
      "description": "Program Manager Student Engagement - Main Campus - Student Affairs Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Program Manager Student Engagement - Main Campus - Student Affairs Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Program Manager Student Engagement 501370 Main Campus - Student Affairs Toledo, OH Administration Administrative Support Full-Time None Student Affairs Show More Show Less Staff - Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Program Manager Student Engagement Department Org: Student Engmt & Connections - 103740 Employee Classification: U1 Bargaining Unit: Professional Staff Association Primary Location: MC SA Shift: 1 Posted Salary: Salary commensurate based on experience Travel: Yes Weekend/Holiday: Yes Job Description: This position within the Office of Student Engagement & Connections (OSEC) helps with the daily operations and running of the office. This role oversees the student staff team including but not limited to: hiring, scheduling, training, and managing their time sheets. This role also assists in the management of the student engagement platform “InvoNet” and processes student organization event requests in conjunction with the Student Union reservationist. This position also helps in the planning and logistics of major university events including: Campus Involvement Fairs, Homecoming, Family weekends, awards banquets, etc. Minimum Qualifications: • Bachelor’s degree required and minimum of one year of related work experience or combination of education and experience • Excellent customer service and public relations • Strong written and verbal communications skills • Ability to work independently or as a team member • Knowledge of and experience with Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Publisher, and Outlook) • Ability to work flexible schedule and sometimes long hours including nights and/or weekends • Knowledge of student organizations Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of hea