    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/private-swim-lessons-group-instructor-main-campus-administration-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states": {
      "title": "Private Swim Lessons & Group Instructor - Main Campus",
      "description": "Private Swim Lessons & Group Instructor - Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Private Swim Lessons & Group Instructor - Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Private Swim Lessons & Group Instructor 501691 Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH None Part-Time Seasonal Student Positions Student Services Show More Show Less Staff - Temporary Add to favorites View favorites Title: Private Swim Lessons & Group Instructor Department Org: Student Rec Center - 104310 Employee Classification: H6 - Intermittent - Seasonal Hourly Bargaining Unit: Bargaining Unit Exempt Primary Location: MC AD Shift: 1 Posted Salary: 16.70 Job Description: Private Swim: • Be familiar with American Red Cross Learn-to-Swim levels and other Red Cross water safety courses, know how to use course materials effectively • Be able to adapt teaching approaches to the age, experience and ability of participants so they can meet course objectives • Maintain a safe and controlled learning environment for all skill levels • Act quickly in the case of an emergency, follow facility specific Emergency Action Plan • Communicate regularly with participants and parents to ensure they are aware of progress • Submit and maintain skill sheets, lesson logs and attendance information in a timely manner • Teach at least one session of group swim lessons and 2 private lessons a semester. • Attend mandatory in-service trainings and meetings • Attend and participate in all trainings and meetings within employee group and department wide Group Instructor: • Administer audits to Office of Recreational Services employees assigned. • Attend and actively participate in all Safety Education in-services and staff meetings. • Respond to emergencies in strict accordance to the Student Recreation Center Emergency Action Plan. • Complete additional duties as assigned by Coordinator, Aquatic & Challenge • Attend and participate in all trainings and meetings within employee group and department wide, including Leadership and Training Week. • Cleaning of mannequins and equipment Minimum Qualifications: Must have currently or the ability upon being hired to be certified from the American Red Cross Lifeguard Instructor, CPR/AED for the Professional Rescuer, or Basic Life Support Instructor certificate. Be proficient in First Aid, CPR/AED, and (if applicable) water skills according to American Red Cross standards. Be able to evaluate and give corrective feedback to participants on skills and grade test at the conclusion of each class. Must be up to date with all skills. Instruct classes of up to 10 participants. Or have or the ability to obtain a Water Safety Instructor certification though the American Red Cross Preferred Qualifications: • American Red Cross Lifeguard Instructor or CPR/BLS Instructor • Lifeguarding/First Aid/CPR-PR/AED or CPR-PR/AED and First Aid or BLS and First Aid or Water Saftey • Attend all UToledo Rec compliance trainings and new employee department and employee group trainings • Successfully complete 30-day probationary employment period Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements for the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center will include drug and other required health screenings for the position. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to attracting and retaining the best and brightest talent and fostering a culture of respect. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact HR Compliance at hrcompliance@utoledo.edu or 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m. or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the Center for Administrative Support on the UToledo Main Campus. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 0c561ced Last Name (required) 214d751a Email (required) 5e8149f8 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 4d81a740 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories None Part-Time Seasonal Student Positions Student Services None Part-Time Seasonal Student Positions Student Services Employment Type Staff - Temporary Staff - Temporary Locations Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States First Name (required) 39ef738c Last Name (required) 03970386 Email (required) bb335641 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
