    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/building-operator-health-science-campus-hospital-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states-b0dc8412-90e8-44df-a37d-2fbf98d430be": {
      "title": "Building Operator",
      "description": "Building Operator - Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Building Operator - Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Building Operator 501646 Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH AFSCME Full-Time Maintenance/Facilities Staff - Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Building Operator Department Org: HVAC-Campus Env & Phy Plnt - 108360 Employee Classification: B1 - Classif'd Full Time AFSCME HSC Bargaining Unit: AFSCME HSC Primary Location: HSC H Shift: 1 Start Time: 7:00am End Time: 3:30pm Posted Salary: $23.15 Float: False Rotate: False On Call: False Travel: False Weekend/Holiday: True Job Description: Under general supervision of appropriate Manager, the Building Operator performs skilled HVAC/R, plumbing, electrical, steam system maintenance & operation, and general housekeeping/maintenance of the assigned buildings or systems. Performs preventative maintenance on all building systems and components. The primary function of the position is to perform, repair, upgrade, schedule and organize the upkeep of the assigned buildings, grounds, facilities, rooms, storage areas, and all of its equipment, services, and vehicles. The Building Operator will ensure the maintenance, safety, cleanliness, and organization of the building, its property, vehicles, and its contents. Minimum Qualifications: • Requires 3-5 years in one (or a combination) of the following fields: HVAC/R, electrical, plumbing and/or general maintenance. • Maintains a valid driver’s license and must be insurable under the University of Toledo’s driving policies • Knowledge of general maintenance and general repair practices • Ability to use math, read and write common vocabulary, read blueprints, understand manuals, and verbal instructions (technical in nature) • Ability to walk, climb, bend, twist, kneel and lift up to 50lbs. Preferred Qualifications: Conditions of Employment: To promote the 