    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/mental-health-tech-health-science-campus-hospital-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states-7580f888-dcf8-458b-a947-a516dc6d81cf": {
      "title": "Mental Health Tech",
      "description": "Mental Health Tech - Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Mental Health Tech - Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Mental Health Tech 501573 Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH AFSCME Full-Time Healthcare Positions Mental Health Show More Show Less Staff - Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Mental Health Tech Department Org: OP-Clinic-Psychiatry - 109630 Employee Classification: B5 - Unclass Full Time AFSCME HSC Bargaining Unit: AFSCME HSC Primary Location: HSC H Shift: 1 Start Time: 8am End Time: 4:30pm Posted Salary: $19.55 - $22.67 Job Description: Provides access to care and information to patients seeking care in the Outpatient Psychiatric Clinics. Contacts Managed Care Organizations and Third-Party Payers to determine Mental Health benefits and interacts with medical and therapeutic staff to schedule patients with the appropriate providers. The ages of patients served spans the spectrum of the life cycle. Care will be directed at taking information from patients, answering questions from patients, visitors, etc. recognizing that every age group has unique developmental characteristics influencing the approach that should be utilized in dealing with these patients. Minimum Qualifications: Education / Knowledge / Skills / Abilities 1. Graduate from an approved school with an Associate Degree in Mental Health Technology or two years of college in Psychology or related field. 2. BLS required. Demonstrates proficient interviewing techniques and empathic interactions appropriate to the emotional wellbeing of the patient. 4. Ability to plan and organize work and to work under close supervision. Willingness to accept responsibility for patients and their care when performing designated functions of this position. 5. May be required to rotate shifts and units. 6. Physical requirements: a. visual acuity of 20/20 or corrected to 20/20 including color vision when applicable; b. ability to hear (with or without aides); c. ability to orally communicate; d. good manual dexterity; e. ability to push, pull, roll, and transfer/lift 50 pounds occasionally; f. ability to stand, walk frequently; g. ability to bend, reach, stoop, kneel frequently; h. ability to perform CPR; and i. must be able to physically hold and restrain patients. Communication/Skills 1. Exhibits accuracy, integrity and flexibility; is punctual and dependable. 2. Possesses organizational, problem-solving, and critical thinking skills. 3. Demonstrates ability to work with self-direction and effectiveness under minimal supervision. 4. Demonstrates excellent written and verbal communication skills; possesses group facilitation skills. 5. Must have demonstrated ability in conflict negotiation and ability to exercise diplomacy and tact in potentially volatile situations. 6. Must be able to tolerate aggressive patients and exposure to both verbal and physical aggression. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to attracting and retaining the best and brightest talent and fostering a culture of respect. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact HR Compliance at hrcompliance@utoledo.edu or 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m. or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the Center for Administrative Support on the UToledo Main Campus. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) b507cc06 Last Name (required) 3a7ec9a6 Email (required) 0f612b40 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 9a46273e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories AFSCME Full-Time Healthcare Positions Mental Health AFSCME Full-Time Healthcare Positions Mental Health Employment Type Staff - Full-Time Staff - Full-Time Locations Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States First Name (required) 8dd30654 Last Name (required) f8f3f803 Email (required) f26c3464 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website