    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/assistant-to-the-chair-health-science-campus-college-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states-bb75dcb5-c5a4-42b3-a43e-0e30c30b2602": {
      "title": "Assistant to the Chair",
      "description": "Assistant to the Chair - Health Science Campus College Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Assistant to the Chair - Health Science Campus College Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Assistant to the Chair 501540 Health Science Campus College Toledo, OH Administration Administrative Support Full-Time None Show More Show Less Staff - Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Assistant to the Chair Department Org: Neurosciences - 107510 Employee Classification: J1 - Salaried Full Time HSC Bargaining Unit: Professional Staff Association Primary Location: HSC C Shift: 1 Start Time: 8:30 a.m. End Time: 5:00 p.m. Salary: Salary will be based on education and experience Job Description: Applicant works with minimal supervision from the department chair and the Department Administrator to plan, direct and manage daily department operations and activities. Applicant will complete duties and responsibilities as described below to provide high-quality, cost-effective management of department administrative and budgetary functions. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor Degree in business administration, management, public relations or other related field required OR 5 year’s office environment experience may be accepted in lieu of degree. Excellent computer skills required. Proficiency in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook). Knowledge of Publisher, Photoshop, Illustrator, Blackboard, and API helpful. Preferred Qualifications: Qualifications/Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Education/experience/licensing: Communication and other skills: Ability to organize, prioritize and efficiently coordinate various responsibilities and job duties. Ability to establish constructive interpersonal relationships. Ability to work independently, be self-motivated, and be proactive to avoid negative consequences. Ability to respond to rapidly changing business environment. Ability to multitask (e.g., preparing grants, budgets and luncheon meetings simultaneously). Ability to maintain high degree of confidentiality. Excellent written, verbal and culturally appropriate communication skills. Analysis, assessment and evaluation skills. Appreciation for scientific research and an understanding of basic science helpful. Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements for the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center will include drug and other required health screenings for the position. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to attracting and retaining the best and brightest talent and fostering a culture of respect. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact HR Compliance at hrcompliance@utoledo.edu or 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m. or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the Center for Administrative Support on the UToledo Main Campus. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) e4623e52 Last Name (required) c1684816 Email (required) 798d342f Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and in