      "description": "Phys Ther Asst Lic I - Health Science Campus Support Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Phys Ther Asst Lic I - Health Science Campus Support Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Phys Ther Asst Lic I 501278 Health Science Campus Support Toledo, OH AFSCME Full-Time Healthcare Positions Staff - Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Physical Therapy Assistant Licensed I Department Org: OP-Physical Therapy - 109320 Employee Classification: B5 - Unclass Full Time AFSCME HSC Bargaining Unit: AFSCME HSC Primary Location: HSC H Shift: 1 Start Time: 7am End Time: 6pm Posted Salary: 22.28-28.34/hour Float: True Rotate: False On Call: False Travel: False Weekend/Holiday: True Job Description: Administers physical therapy treatments and related duties under the working direction of, and as assistant to, the physical therapist. Minimum Qualifications: Education/experience/licensing: • Successful completion of at least a 2-year college program for Physical Therapy Assistants that leads to an associate’s degree and has been approved by APTA. • Current physical therapy assistant licensure from the Ohio Board of Occupational Therapy, Physical Therapy, and Athletic Trainers or a licensure applicant • Maintains the standards set by the American Physical Therapy Association regarding treatment procedure and professional ethics • Evidence of appropriate academic and clinical preparation for patient care in Physical Therapy Services at Medical College of Ohio • Knowledge of The Laws and Rules Governing the Practice of Physical Therapy. • Ability to pass annual safety test. • Obtains/maintains CPR Certification from the American Heart Association prior to the completion of probationary period. American Red Cross CPR Certification is acceptable for hire. • Ability to achieve competencies for assigned work area ( i.e., age specific, suctioning, CPR, etc.) Preferred Qualifications: Interest in treatment of neurological diagnoses. Conditions 