    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/clinical-assistant-lecturer-main-campus-academic-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Lecturer - Main Campus",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant Lecturer - Main Campus - Academic Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Clinical Assistant Lecturer - Main Campus - Academic Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Clinical Assistant Lecturer 501577 Main Campus - Academic Toledo, OH Academic Faculty - Regular Add to favorites View favorites Title: Clinical Assistant Lecturer Department Org: Pharmacy Practice - 102210 Employee Classification: FF - Faculty Lecturer 12 Month Bargaining Unit: Lecturer`s Unit Job Description: The Clinical Assistant Lecturer will teach in the College of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences (CPPS) PharmD program and will work collaboratively with one of the interprofessional inpatient teams within The University of Toledo Medical Center. Job duties and responsibilities include in-classroom teaching, patient care, scholarly activity, and service. The Clinical Assistant Lecturer will teach in the classroom and skills-based laboratory portions of the didactic curriculum, precept entry level Doctor of Pharmacy students (IPPEs and APPEs) and PGY1 residents, and will advise students. The individual will also round with interprofessional teams at The University of Toledo Medical Center (UTMC). Patient care responsibilities include medication review and reconciliation, medication selection and dosing recommendations, therapeutic drug monitoring, provision of drug information, and patient education. The Clinical Assistant Lecturer will also be responsible for nurse, physician, and pharmacy staff development; coordinating and conducting quality initiative projects; and developing collaborative treatment protocols. Scholarly activities, including presentations and publications, are encouraged and will be supported. More information about the College and the Department of Pharmacy Practice can be found at www.utoledo.edu/pharmacy. Job location: · The University of Toledo, College of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences, Wolfe Center-Health Education Building, 3000 Arlington Ave., Toledo, OH, 43614 · The University of Toledo Medical Center, 3000 Arlington Ave., Toledo, OH, 43614 Start date: · As soon as possible Minimum Qualifications: · Doctor of Pharmacy degree from an ACPE-accredited program · Completion of Postgraduate Year 1 (PGY1) or equivalent residency training. · Some research and scholarly activity experience is expected. · Licensed, or eligible for licensure, to practice pharmacy in Ohio. Must be eligible for employment in the United States. Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements for the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center will include drug and other required health screenings for the position. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to attracting and retaining the best and brightest talent and fostering a culture of respect. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact HR Compliance at hrcompliance@utoledo.edu or 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m. or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the Center for Administrative Support on the UToledo Main Campus. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 363a82ab Last Name (required) f0951514 Email (required) 91fadfc3 Refer s