    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/student-admissions-counselor-2-main-campus-administration-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states": {
      "title": "Student Admissions Counselor 2 - Main Campus",
      "description": "Student Admissions Counselor 2 - Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Student Admissions Counselor 2 - Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Student Admissions Counselor 2 501642 Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH Academic Administrative Support CWA Enrollment Full-Time Student Services Support Services Show More Show Less Staff - Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Student Admissions Counselor 2 Department Org: Undergraduate Admission - 103180 Employee Classification: H3 - Comm Workers of America FT Bargaining Unit: Communication Workers America Primary Location: MC AD Shift: 1 Start Time: 8:15am End Time: 5:00pm Posted Salary: Starting at $23.19 Job Description: This role contributes to the fulfillment of the University's mission and vision by serving as a territory/population lead for a specified recruitment region/focus. This position will research assigned territories/populations in order to plan and facilitate strategies to attract potential students to apply to the University. This position will offer assistance to individual students with regard to the admission process. Use data-driven methods to determine within the assigned territory/population, which high schools, community colleges, cities and fairs in which to recruit. Identify prospective students who meet The University of Toledo student profile while building relationships with major influencers including parents, high school counselors, community members, community college partners, influential alumni, etc. Minimum Qualifications: • Bachelor’s Degree • Two years of progressively responsible experience in admissions, enrollment management, recruitment, higher education, sales, marketing, or a related field. • Strong organizational, project management, and problem-solving skills. • Strong verbal, written, and interpersonal skills. • Ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines in a fast-paced environment. • Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite, CRM platforms, and other technology systems used to support recruitment and enrollment operations. • Commitment to providing excellent service and fostering a welcoming and supportive environment for all prospective students and families. • Ability to travel, including Preferred Qualifications: • Experience planning, implementing, and assessing recruitment, enrollment, outreach, and student engagement initiatives. • Knowledge of adult, dual enrollment, international, military-affiliated, online, and/or transfer admissions. • Experience using enrollment management systems, student information systems, and Constituent Relationship Management (CRM) platforms. • Demonstrated experience leading projects, facilitating training, mentoring peers, or coordinating programs or initiatives. • Demonstrated ability to build and maintain effective relationships with students, families, school counselors, community partners, faculty, and staff. Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements for the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center will include drug and other required health screenings for the position. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to attracting and retaining the best and brightest talent and fostering a culture of respect. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact HR Compliance at hrcompliance@utoledo.edu or 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m. or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the Center for Administrative Support on the UToledo Main Campus. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 0b15b408 Last Name (required) bee1ff3e Email (required) b6f75167 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 06aa79a3 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Academic Administrative Support CWA Enrollment Full-Time Student Services Support Services Academic Administrative Support CWA Enrollment Full-Time Student Servic