    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/seasonal-employee-hourly-main-campus-academic-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states-aba902ba-5db2-4a97-9c55-12996227e113": {
      "title": "Seasonal Employee Hourly - Main Campus",
      "description": "Seasonal Employee Hourly - Main Campus - Academic Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Seasonal Employee Hourly - Main Campus - Academic Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Seasonal Employee Hourly 501659 Main Campus - Academic Toledo, OH Academic Administration Administrative Support None Part-Time Show More Show Less Staff - Part-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Seasonal Employee Hourly Department Org: Electrical Engineering - 101990 Employee Classification: H6 - Intermittent - Seasonal Hourly Bargaining Unit: Bargaining Unit Exempt Primary Location: MC AC Shift: 1 Start Time: End Time: Posted Salary: 12.00 Float: no Rotate: no On Call: no Travel: no Weekend/Holiday: no Job Description: The individual in this position will support research and development activities focused on the performance measurement, analysis, and optimization of High-Performance Computing (HPC) workflows in cloud computing environments. Responsibilities include evaluating workflow performance, developing and testing resource management and scheduling solutions, analyzing system efficiency and scalability, and assisting with the design and implementation of workflow management systems for cloud-based HPC applications. The position offers hands-on experience with cloud computing, distributed systems, performance benchmarking, and advanced computing technologies while contributing to cutting-edge research in HPC resource scheduling and workflow optimization. Minimum Qualifications: • Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science • Experience with C/C++ programming • Experience with command-line or shell programming • Understanding of distributed systems, parallel computing, or High-Performance Computing (HPC) concepts • Strong problem-solving and analytical skills • Ability to evaluate options and develop solutions • Excellent written and verbal communication skills • Confident, articulate, and professional speaking abilities Preferred Qualifications: • Experience with cloud computing platforms or cloud-based computing environments • Experience with High-Performance Computing workflows • Knowledge of resource management and scheduling techniques • Experience conducting performance testing, benchmarking, and system analysis • Ability to analyze execution time, resource utilization, scalability, throughput, and cost efficiency • Familiarity with workflow management systems • Knowledge of HPC resource scheduling and workflow optimization • Experience working with computationally intensive scientific, engineering, or data-driven applications The individual may report to a faculty member daily while having a dotted line to the Department Chair. Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements for the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center will include drug and other required health screenings for the position. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to attracting and retaining the best and brightest talent and fostering a culture of respect. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact HR Compliance at hrcompliance@utoledo.edu or 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m. or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the