    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/histotechnologist-htl-health-science-campus-hospital-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states-92e93e45-a359-4316-9e2c-ddafecd8bc3b": {
      "title": "Histotechnologist HTL",
      "description": "Histotechnologist HTL - Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Histotechnologist HTL - Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Histotechnologist HTL 501641 Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH AFSCME Full-Time Healthcare Positions Staff - Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Histotechnologist HTL Department Org: Lab-Histology - 109410 Employee Classification: B5 - Unclass Full Time AFSCME HSC Bargaining Unit: AFSCME HSC Primary Location: HSC H Shift: 1 Start Time: 0500 End Time: 1700 Posted Salary: $33.37 - $40.61 Float: False Rotate: True On Call: True Travel: False Weekend/Holiday: True Job Description: This position requires an individual to perform routine histological functions including specimen handling, accessioning, processing, embedding, cutting, H&E staining and labeling of slides, blocks and specimen containers, low and high complexity histochemical staining, immunohistochemical staining, kidney biopsy procedures, muscle biopsy procedures, nerve biopsy procedures, immunofluorescent staining and teaching and training of residents, medical students, histotechnologists, histotechnicians, and staff. This position may also require an individual to document daily routine maintenance, file slides/blocks accurately, change chemicals routinely, accession specimens, and perform low complexity special stains. Minimum Qualifications: • A minimum of an Bachelor’s Degree with a combined thirty-six (36) credit hours in a Science-related field including six (6) hours of Biology and six (6) hours of Chemistry is required. • HTL (ASCP) required. Eligibility for certification may be acceptable with the understanding that certification will be required within the probationary period (180 days). • Knowledge of The Joint Commission, CAP, FDA regulatory standards and guidelines as applicable. • Ability to effectively solve multiple problems and troubleshooting preferred. • Shows high level of professional competence, discretion and judgement. Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements for the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center will include drug and other required health screenings for the position. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to attracting and retaining the best and brightest talent and fostering a culture of respect. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact HR Compliance at hrcompliance@utoledo.edu or 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m. or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the Center for Administrative Support on the UToledo Main Campus. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 2d27b686 Last Name (required) 13daec47 Email (required) 9ed634e9 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. ED Registration Specialist Hea