    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/workers-compensation-risk-manager-main-campus-administration-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states": {
      "title": "Workers Compensation & Risk Manager - Main Campus",
      "description": "Workers Compensation & Risk Manager - Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Workers Compensation & Risk Manager - Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Workers Compensation & Risk Manager 501652 Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH Academic Administration Administrative Support Full-Time Management None Show More Show Less Staff - Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Workers Compensation & Risk Manager Department Org: Risk Management - 110510 Employee Classification: U1 - Unclassified PSA FT Bargaining Unit: Professional Staff Association Primary Location: MC AD Shift: 1 Start Time: 8:00 End Time: 5:00 Posted Salary: Salary commensurate with education and experience Float: {bOther1} Rotate: {bOther2} On Call: {bOther3} Travel: {bOther4} Weekend/Holiday: {bOther5} Job Description: Responsible for developing, maintaining, and managing The University of Toledo’s Workers’ Compensation Program. Implements all matters of the program including but not limited to claim investigation and processing, Third Party Administrator (TPA) and Managed Care Organization (MCO) oversight, and litigation in a manner which promotes the UToledo mission of improving the human condition. Manages the day-to-day activities of all workers’ compensation claims for all University Campuses. This task includes: interaction between Ohio Bureau of Workers’ Compensation, TPA and MCO; facilitating transitional/modified duty program; analyzing and investigating injury reports for compensability; assisting legal counsel at the Industrial Commission; reviewing claims for settlement potential; making recommendations to Health & Safety for training based on injury trends; and updating Human Resources personnel on work comp leaves of absence. Assists the Director of Risk Management & Insurance with coordinating the University’s risk management and insurance programs, identifying potential risks, and supporting efforts to prevent or reduce losses. Minimum Qualifications: • Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration, Public Administration, Risk Management or a directly related field, plus three (3) years of work experience administering and adjusting workers’ compensation claims. Will accept an equivalency of 7 years of direct workers compensation management. • Comprehensive knowledge of the Ohio Workers’ Compensation system, law/rules, actuarial processes and claims management procedures. • Strong analytical, time management and organizational skills. • Knowledge of regarding changing legislation, BWC and Industrial Commission policies and procedures accordingly. • Deep understanding of state and federal workers' compensation statutes, employment laws (like ADA and FMLA), and OSHA reporting mandates. • Familiarity with claims administration best practices, medical terminology, reserving procedures, and risk management principles. • Ability to build trusted relationships across all organizational tiers and navigate emotionally charged or difficult situations with empathy. • High-level ability to maintain strict confidentiality regarding sensitive employee and medical information. • Exceptional written and oral communication skills to explain complex claim processes to injured workers and present data to leadership Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements for the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center will include drug and other required health screenings for the position. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to attracting and retaining the best and brightest talent and fostering a culture of respect. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact HR Compliance at hrcompliance@utoledo.edu or 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m. or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the Center for Administrative Support on the UToledo Main Campus. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 2c7bce6a Last Name (required) 1da46e37 Email (required) 4d15b849 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 9c0cd88c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You 