    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/electrician-journeyman-main-campus-administration-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states": {
      "title": "Electrician Journeyman - Main Campus",
      "description": "Electrician Journeyman - Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Electrician Journeyman - Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Electrician Journeyman 501558 Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH CWA Full-Time Maintenance/Facilities Staff - Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Electrician Journeyman Department Org: Maintenance/Electric - 105580 Employee Classification: H3 - Comm Workers of America FT Bargaining Unit: Communication Workers America Primary Location: MC AD Shift: 1 Start Time: 7:00am End Time: 3:30pm Posted Salary: Up to $35.03 Float: False Rotate: False On Call: False Travel: False Weekend/Holiday: False Job Description: Under general supervision of the Manager, Electrical Maintenance, performs skilled repairs on all electrical instruments and control equipment or systems and components, including the 12,470-volt substation and associated loop system. Performs necessary maintenance on outdoor site lighting and assists with the testing of the generators and associated reporting. Performs preventative maintenance and repairs on all building systems and components. The incumbent is responsible for meeting work schedules, service request, preparing work orders, and ordering necessary parts by providing efficient maintenance workmanship and leadership. Oversee the one-the-job training of apprentice(s). Minimum Qualifications: • Must possess a High School diploma or equivalent GED. • Department of Labor or equivalent journeyman Electrician certificate or associate degree or technical school certificate and five (5) or more years related experience. • Knowledge of related building codes required. • Knowledge of general maintenance and general repair practices of building components • Must be able to bend, stand, kneel, climb ladders and stairs and perform manual work that requires dexterity. • Maintain a valid driver’s license and must be insurable under UT driving policies. • May be required to lift 50 pounds. Preferred Qualifications: Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements for the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center will include drug and other required health screenings for the position. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to attracting and retaining the best and brightest talent and fostering a culture of respect. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact HR Compliance at hrcompliance@utoledo.edu or 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m. or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the Center for Administrative Support on the UToledo Main Campus. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 22a99abe Last Name (required) 4e38987a Email (required) d5e2ac6a Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. ED Registration Special