    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/assistant-associate-or-full-professor-hematology-oncology-health-science-campus-college-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor - Hematology/Oncology",
      "description": "Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor - Hematology/Oncology - Health Science Campus College Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor - Hematology/Oncology - Health Science Campus College Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor - Hematology/Oncology 500923 Health Science Campus College Toledo, OH Academic Full-Time Healthcare Positions Faculty - Regular Add to favorites View favorites Job Description: UToledo Health and the University of Toledo College of Medicine and Life Sciences has an academic faculty position opening for a Hematology/Oncology Physician in the Department of Medicine. The Division of Hematology Oncology provides patient care in the inpatient and outpatient setting, teaching of medical students, residents and fellows, as well as opportunities for research. We seek a diverse pool of applicants who wish to join an academic community that places the highest value on rigorous inquiry and encourages diverse perspectives and experiences. The physician hired will have a faculty appointment at the University of Toledo College of Medicine and Life Sciences with the appointment commensurate with the candidate's credentials. Position Highlights: Benign and malignant hematology and medical oncology practice in both inpatient and outpatient settings Practice within an academic teaching hospital, working with hematology/medical oncology fellows, resident, and medical students Presence of local multidisciplinary tumor boards and collaborative specialty and subspecialty services Opportunity to participate in clinical and/or basic research Opportunity to participate in program development and quality initiatives Strong referral network throughout Northwest Ohio and Southeast Michigan in addition to primary care practices through UToledo Health Competitive compensation package with comprehensive benefits Responsibilities: Provide benign and malignant hematology and medical oncology care through diagnosis, treatment, management and surveillance Management of inpatient, primarily through consultations for hematology/medical oncology, in rotation with division colleagues Adhere to departmental policies, quality improvement initiatives, safety standards, infection-control practices, and institutional objectives. Participate in educational programs within the Division of Hematology/Oncology, Department of Medicine within the College of Medicine and Life Sciences, at the University of Toledo Engage in clinical research Minimum Qualifications: MD or equivalent required Successful completion of an Internal Medicine residency Fellowship trained in Hematology Oncology Board certified or board eligible by the American Board of Internal Medicine in Hematology Oncology Current licensure in the State of Ohio required, prior to beginning the position Benefits: Retirement Benefits, including two pension plans UTP has a pension plan with employer contribution. UT Academic pension Eligibility for health, dental, vision, and life insurance coverage through the University of Toledo Paid time off, paid parental and maternity leave UT provides a Tuition Fee Waiver Program for Employees and Dependents Long Term and Short-Term Disability UTP opts out of FICA, reducing the employee's payroll taxes About Toledo, Ohio: The city of Toledo is located in NW Ohio near the western point of Lake Erie and along the Maumee River. Being the 4th largest city in Ohio, Toledo continues to grow as it is home to over 200,000 residents. There is much to see and do as it is home to 19 large metro parks with over 120 miles to bike, walk, and hike along the trails. Downtown Toledo is the hub for entertainment, as you can visit the Toledo Museum of Art, the Toledo Zoo, and the Toledo Symphony Orchestra! The city also partakes in numerous sports activities, from minor league baseball, golfing clubs, and hockey, which can all be found within a few miles of each other. Toledo continues to be one of the most affordable places to live in the region. There are many different living options, from lofts in downtown to comfortable suburbs and villas. Toledo holds many high-quality schools and universities open for parents and students. Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. To further this effort, the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center is requiring candidates for employment to be nicotine-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements will include cotinine (nicotine) testing, as well as drug and other required health screenings for the position. With the exception of positions within University of Toledo Main Campus and the University of Toledo College of Medicine and Life Sciences, the employment offer is conditional upon successful completion of a cotinine test and Occupational Health clearance. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to the goal of building a culturally diverse and pluralistic faculty and staff committed to teaching and working in a multicultural environment and strongly encourages applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, dual-career professionals and covered veterans. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact the Human Resources Department at 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30AM and 5:00PM or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the Center for Administrative Support on the Main Campus of the University of Toledo. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) af66b860 Last Name (required) 2b54948b Email (required) bb782d70 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 084abbaf Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Academic Full-Time Healthcare Positions Academic Full-Time Healthcare Positions Employment Type Faculty - Regular Faculty - Regular Locations Health Science Campus College Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Health Science Campus College Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States First Name (required) 0954f275 Last Name 