    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/senior-payroll-analyst-main-campus-administration-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states": {
      "title": "Senior Payroll Analyst - Main Campus",
      "description": "Senior Payroll Analyst - Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Senior Payroll Analyst - Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Senior Payroll Analyst 501201 Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH Administration Administrative Support Full-Time None Show More Show Less Staff - Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Senior Payroll Analyst Department Org: Controller - 106250 Employee Classification: U1 - Unclassified PSA FT Bargaining Unit: Professional Staff Association Primary Location: MC AD Shift: 1 Start Time: 8:00 AM End Time: 5:00 PM Posted Salary: $60,500 - $75,000 Float: False Rotate: False On Call: False Travel: False Weekend/Holiday: False Job Description: The Senior Payroll Analyst contributes to the fulfillment of the university's mission and vision by ensuring system functionality and compliance with all applicable laws, rules, and regulations. The Senior Payroll Analyst responsibilities include but are not limited to exercising discretion and professional judgment in examining and evaluating payroll; managing the accounting and reconciliation, recording, monitoring, and reporting of all payroll related accounts; interacting with staff to accurately and timely process payroll including review, verification, and reconciliation of each payroll; reviewing and approving payroll tax processing, adjustments, and other payroll related requests as needed; assisting the Fiscal Manager in the supervision of the payroll staff; and in identifying and implementing continuous process improvements. Minimum Qualifications: •Bachelor’s degree required in Accounting, Finance, related business, or technical degree. •Minimum of 5 years of directly related work experience in Payroll, Accounting, Audit, or Finance with working knowledge of payroll tax rules, regulations and general accounting with problem solving and process improvement skills required. •Requires analysis and judgment in accomplishing diversified duties and the exercise of independent thinking within the limits of policies and regulations. •Proficiency with Microsoft Office, accounting applications, system query capabilities, PC based spreadsheet, and database software for analyzing and forecasting required. •Requires strong research, communication, and customer service skills. Preferred Qualifications: •Master’s degree in business, HR, Accounting, or related field preferred. •Experience in a large university or governmental/non-profit organization preferred. •Banner, Symplr and Sprintax systems experience a plus •At least one year’s experience in supervision or management preferred. Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements for the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center will include drug and other required health screenings for the position. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to attracting and retaining the best and brightest talent and fostering a culture of respect. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact HR Compliance at hrcompliance@utoledo.edu or 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m. or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the Center for