    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/director-of-government-relations-and-community-engagement-main-campus-administration-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states": {
      "title": "Director of Government Relations and Community Engagement - Main Campus",
      "description": "Director of Government Relations and Community Engagement - Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Director of Government Relations and Community Engagement - Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Director of Government Relations and Community Engagement 501135 Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH Administration Full-Time Management Marketing/Communication None Show More Show Less Staff - Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Director of Government Relations and Community Engagement Department Org: Government Relations - 100410 Employee Classification: U1 - Unclassified PSA FT Bargaining Unit: Professional Staff Association Primary Location: MC AD Shift: 1 Posted Salary: Salary commensurate with experience Job Description: Leads the Office of Government Relations and Community Engagement. Serves as the chief government relations officer for UToledo spanning local, state and federal government relationships and provides key insights to and oversees UToledo’s contract lobbyists. In consultation with the President and President’s Cabinet, directs UToledo's Government Relations activities at the local, state and federal levels. Responsibilities include planning and development of the institution's response to proposed legislation; developing and maintaining effective relationships with government agencies and officials; analyzing, assessing and advocating on legislative, administrative, and regulatory government activities as they pertain to UToledo programs including academic, research, athletics, and health care programs, activities and operations; and communicating these activities and information to internal and external stakeholders in partnership with UToledo’s contract lobbyists. Oversee community engagement for UToledo including University sponsorships, partnerships, events and programming to align with the strategic priorities of the University. Minimum Qualifications: Education/experience/licensing: • A master’s or advanced degree in political science, public policy or law or significant experience in government or higher education required. • At least 7 years’ experience working in government relations; or a university office with a major portion of responsibility relating to government relations and/or community engagement. • Minimum of five years of supervisory experience is required with seven preferred. • Experience serving as the primary point person for visits of high political office (governor, senators, members of the House of Representatives, White House visitors including cabinet holders, and senior agency officials at the state and federal level). Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements for the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center will include drug and other required health screenings for the position. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to attracting and retaining the best and brightest talent and fostering a culture of respect. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact HR Compliance at hrcompliance@utoledo.edu or 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m. or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the Center for Administrative Support on the UToledo Main Campus. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) b8034aeb Last Name (required) acf17ab8 Email (required) 1b177561 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert f0c0d138 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administration Full-Time Management Marketing/Communication None Administration Full-Time Management Marketing/Communication None Employment Type Staff - Full-Time Staff - Full-Time Locations Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Main Campus - Administration Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States First Name (required) 85a29884 Last Name (required) f8b8ac8f Email (required) 88306c84 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidat