    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/assistant-associate-or-full-professor-general-urologist-health-science-campus-college-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor - General Urologist",
      "description": "Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor - General Urologist - Health Science Campus College Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor - General Urologist - Health Science Campus College Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor - General Urologist 501260 Health Science Campus College Toledo, OH Academic Faculty Full-Time Healthcare Positions None Show More Show Less Faculty - Regular Job Description: UToledo Health and the University of Toledo College of Medicine and Life Sciences have a faculty position opening for a General Urologist in the Department of Urology. This position offers the opportunity to provide comprehensive urologic care while contributing to the education of future physicians and advancing the academic mission of the institution. Clinical Responsibilities Provide comprehensive evaluation, diagnosis, and treatment of patients with general urologic conditions. Perform outpatient and inpatient consultations. Perform office-based procedures as well as endoscopic, laparoscopic, open, and robotic-assisted surgical procedures, as appropriate. Participate in operating room coverage and inpatient rounding. Share an equitable call schedule with members of the Department of Urology. Provide urologic services at satellite practice locations as needed. Maintain accurate, timely, and complete documentation in the electronic medical record. Meet departmental expectations for quality, patient safety, and clinical productivity. Teaching Responsibilities Educate and supervise medical students, residents, fellows, and advanced practice providers. Participate in educational conferences, lectures, journal clubs, and departmental meetings. Provide mentorship to trainees and junior faculty, as appropriate. Academic & Research Responsibilities Participate in clinical research, quality improvement initiatives, and scholarly activities. Contribute to publications, presentations, and academic projects aligned with individual interests and departmental goals. Support the academic mission of the College of Medicine and Life Sciences. Administrative Responsibilities Participate in departmental committees and faculty meetings. Complete required institutional training and maintain compliance with University and hospital policies. Support departmental strategic initiatives and ongoing quality improvement efforts. Benefits: Eligibility for Health, Dental, Vision, and Life Insurance Coverage through the University of Toledo Retirement Benefits, including two Pension Plans: UTP Pension Plan with Employer Contribution UT Academic Pension Paid Time Off, Holidays, Sick Leave, Paid Maternity and Parental Leave UT provided Tuition Fee Waiver Program for Employee and Dependent(s) Long Term and Short-Term Disability UTP opts out of FICA, reducing the employee's payroll taxes Minimum Qualifications: MD or DO degree from an accredited medical school Completion of an ACGME-accredited Urology Residency Program or equivalent training that meets eligibility requirements for board certification and medical licensure in the United States. ECFMG certification, if applicable Board Certified or Board Eligible in Urology Eligible for unrestricted medical licensure in the State of Ohio Eligible for medical staff appointment and clinical privileges at the University of Toledo Medical Center and affiliated hospitals Demonstrated commitment to providing exceptional patient-centered care and maintaining the highest standards of professionalism Preferred Qualifications: Fellowship training is welcomed but not required Experience with robotic-assisted urologic surgery Familiarity with renal transplantation is desirable but not required Interest in resident and medical student education Interest in clinical research and quality improvement initiatives Previous academic practice experience is preferred About Toledo, Ohio: The city of Toledo is located in NW Ohio near the western point of Lake Erie and along the Maumee River. Being the 4th largest city in Ohio, Toledo continues to grow as it is home to over 200,000 residents. There is much to see and do as it is home to 19 large metro parks with over 120 miles to bike, walk, and hike along the trails. Downtown Toledo is the hub for entertainment, as you can visit the Toledo Museum of Art, the Toledo Zoo, and the Toledo Symphony Orchestra! The city also partakes in numerous sports activities, from minor league baseball, golfing clubs, and hockey, which can all be found within a few miles of each other. Toledo continues to be one of the most affordable places to live in the region. There are many different living options, from lofts downtown to comfortable suburbs and villas. Toledo holds many high-quality schools and universities open for parents and students. Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements for the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center will include drug and other required health screenings for the position. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to attracting and retaining the best and brightest talent and fostering a culture of respect. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact HR Compliance at hrcompliance@utoledo.edu or 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m. or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the Center for Administrative Support on the UToledo Main Campus. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 4d2db4e1 Last Name (required) 95012a44 Email (required) acd2b8e1 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert d42f2a8f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Academic Faculty Full-Time Healthcare Positions None Academic Faculty Full-Time Healthcare Positions None Employment Type Faculty - Regular Faculty - Regular Locations Health Science Campus College Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Health Science Campus College Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States First Name (requir