    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/clinical-dietitian-1-health-science-campus-hospital-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states-d7ecce18-5732-4d6e-9323-668ffba48643": {
      "title": "Clinical Dietitian 1",
      "description": "Clinical Dietitian 1 - Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Clinical Dietitian 1 - Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Clinical Dietitian 1 500494 Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH AFSCME Full-Time Healthcare Positions Staff - Full-Time Title: Clinical Dietitian 1 Department Org: Clinical Dieticians - 109770 Employee Classification: B5 Bargaining Unit: AFSCME HSC Primary Location: HSC H Shift: 1 Start Time: 7:30 am End Time: 5:30 pm Posted Salary: $26.42 - $33.36/hr Float: True Rotate: False On Call: True Travel: True Weekend/Holiday: True Job Description: The clinical dietitian is responsible for the nutritional care of in-patients and out-patients. Duties include assessment of nutrition status, development of care plans, follow up, education, and nutrition related order writing privileges. Clinical Dietitian will assure appropriate and continual care of patients through verbal communication with members of the health care team as well as written documentation in the medical record. Care provided is tailored to patient needs including learning needs, age-specific and addresses cultural/religious considerations. Minimum Qualifications: Education/experience/licensing: • Bachelor’s degree in dietetics or food and nutrition with completion of dietetic internship. Master’s degree and membership in Academy of Nutrition and Dietetics preferred. • Completion and maintenance of registration as a dietitian as provided for by the Commission on Dietetic Registration through the Academy of Nutrition and Dietetics. Will accept eligibility to complete Registration provided it is completed within 3 months of hire. • Licensed in state of Ohio to practice dietetics as provided by the State of Ohio Medical Board. • One year work experience in hospital setting as RD, LD preferred. Specialty certification in nutrition support, renal, oncology, gerontology or diabetes education desirable. • Demonstrates competency in the nutritional care of patients including age specific, learning and cultural/religious needs. • Adheres to the standards of professional practice as defined by the Academy of Nutrition and Dietetics Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements for the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center will include drug and other required health screenings for the position. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to attracting and retaining the best and brightest talent and fostering a culture of respect. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact HR Compliance at hrcompliance@utoledo.edu or 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m. or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the Center for Administrative Support on the UToledo Main Campus. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 276f9bd4 Last Name (required) b9ea69f3 Email (required) 1c1f4b27 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert f8c54586 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories AFSCME Full-Time Healthcare Positions AFSCME Full-Time Healthcare Positions Employment Type Staff - Full-Time Staff - Full-Time Locations Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States First Name (required) 13f4745c Last Name (required) eba3e17e Email (required) 87b0e44f Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
