    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/assistant-associate-or-full-professor-family-medicine-health-science-campus-college-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states-9c96fb3a-e1c7-4e25-9ce4-023aa700a85d": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor - Family Medicine",
      "description": "Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor - Family Medicine - Health Science Campus College Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor - Family Medicine - Health Science Campus College Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor - Family Medicine 500863 Health Science Campus College Toledo, OH Academic Faculty Full-Time Healthcare Positions None Show More Show Less Faculty - Regular Job Description: UToledo Health and the University of Toledo College of Medicine and Life Sciences has an academic faculty position opening for a Family Medicine Physician in the Department of Family Medicine. The Department of Family Medicine at the University of Toledo invites applications for a faculty position at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. The selected physician will provide clinical inpatient and outpatient care in a University of Toledo Medical Center–designated practice site and deliver professional medical services on behalf of the University, consistent with the standards of Family Medicine and the highest level of professional competence. Position Highlights: Schedule consists of Monday-Friday, 8:00am-5:00pm with optional evenings and Saturday appointments Clinical education opportunity - 70% clinical time, 30% teaching time 30 minute appointments for patients Responsibilities: Maintain accurate records for all professional services, including required reports, claims, and correspondence Adhere to the American Medical Association principles of medical ethics and comply with all applicable federal and state laws and regulations Follow all University policies and procedures, including proper documentation and coding, HIPAA compliance, and patient privacy requirements Uphold the highest standards of patient care, respect patient needs and expectations, and collaborate effectively with the health care team Provide clinical instruction to medical students and residents, regularly evaluate performance, deliver timely verbal and written feedback, and document achievement of required competencies Minimum Qualifications: MD or equivalent required Successful completion of a Family Medicine residency Current license in the state of Ohio, prior to beginning the position Benefits: Retirement Benefits, including two pension plans UTP has a pension plan with employer contribution. UT Academic pension Eligibility for health, dental, vision, and life insurance coverage through the University of Toledo Paid time off, paid parental and maternity leave UT provides a Tuition Fee Waiver Program for Employees and Dependents Long Term and Short-Term Disability UTP opts out of FICA, reducing the employee's payroll taxes About Toledo, Ohio: The city of Toledo is located in NW Ohio near the western point of Lake Erie and along the Maumee River. Being the 4th largest city in Ohio, Toledo continues to grow as it is home to over 200,000 residents. There is much to see and do as it is home to 19 large metro parks with over 120 miles to bike, walk, and hike along the trails. Downtown Toledo is the hub for entertainment, as you can visit the Toledo Museum of Art, the Toledo Zoo, and the Toledo Symphony Orchestra! The city also partakes in numerous sports activities, from minor league baseball, golfing clubs, and hockey, which can all be found within a few miles of each other. Toledo continues to be one of the most affordable places to live in the region. There are many different living options, from lofts in downtown to comfortable suburbs and villas. Toledo holds many high-quality schools and universities open for parents and students. Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements for the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center will include drug and other required health screenings for the position. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to attracting and retaining the best and brightest talent and fostering a culture of respect. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact HR Compliance at hrcompliance@utoledo.edu or 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m. or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the Center for Administrative Support on the UToledo Main Campus. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) b3720639 Last Name (required) b9f04725 Email (required) dbfe2bb3 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820