    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/instructor-pathologists-assistant-health-science-campus-college-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states": {
      "title": "Instructor/Pathologists' Assistant",
      "description": "Instructor/Pathologists' Assistant - Health Science Campus College Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Instructor/Pathologists' Assistant - Health Science Campus College Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Instructor/Pathologists' Assistant 501078 Health Science Campus College Toledo, OH Academic Faculty Full-Time None Show More Show Less Faculty - Regular Title: Instructor/Pathologists' Assistant Department Org: Pathology - 107610 Employee Classification: A1 - Faculty Full Time 12 Mth HSC Bargaining Unit: Other Non AAUP Primary Location: HSC C Shift: 1 Start Time: End Time: Posted Salary: Float: {bOther1} Rotate: {bOther2} On Call: {bOther3} Travel: {bOther4} Weekend/Holiday: {bOther5} Job Description: This position serves as the Educational Coordinator of the Pathologists' Assistant Program and is responsible for assisting the Program Director in the organization, development, planning and general effectiveness of the Pathologists' Assistant program. In addition, this individual assists in the performance of surgical pathology and autopsy services and is able to work independently when performing professional duties associated with the preparation, performance, and completion of autopsies, and examination and/or preparations of the surgical pathology specimens, with general supervision of a pathologist. Minimum Qualifications: • Graduate of a NAACLS-accredited (AAPA approved prior to 1995) Pathologists' Assistant educational program with an advanced degree (masters or doctoral) • Currently holds ASCP-BOC or ASCPi-BOC certification as a Pathologists' Assistant Preferred Qualifications: • Has practical knowledge of educational methods, and current accreditation and certification procedures Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements for the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center will include drug and other required health screenings for the position. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to attracting and retaining the best and brightest talent and fostering a culture of respect. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact HR Compliance at hrcompliance@utoledo.edu or 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m. or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the Center for Administrative Support on the UToledo Main Campus. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 14bd3382 Last Name (required) df98b2fc Email (required) 085ce3c1 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. ED Registration Speciali