    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/assistant-dean-for-comls-office-of-student-affairs-health-science-campus-college-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Dean for COMLS Office of Student Affairs",
      "description": "Assistant Dean for COMLS Office of Student Affairs - Health Science Campus College Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Assistant Dean for COMLS Office of Student Affairs - Health Science Campus College Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Assistant Dean for COMLS Office of Student Affairs 501122 Health Science Campus College Toledo, OH Academic Administration Advising Faculty None Part-Time Student Affairs Show More Show Less Faculty - Part Time Title: Assistant Dean Department Org: Student Affairs - 108030 Employee Classification: A2 - Faculty Part Time 12 Mth HSC Bargaining Unit: Other Non AAUP Primary Location: HSC C Shift: 1 Start Time: End Time: Posted Salary: Float: {bOther1} Rotate: {bOther2} On Call: {bOther3} Travel: {bOther4} Weekend/Holiday: {bOther5} Job Description: The Assistant Dean provides senior leadership for the Health Science Campus and the University as a whole across a broad spectrum of responsibilities. Principal Duties and Responsibilities •Academic Advisor for ~ 700 medical students •Career Counseling and Advising, including Medical Specialty Decision-Making, Curriculum Vitae and Personal Statement Guidance and Review, Program Selection, and Interviewing Skills •Medical Student Performance Evaluations for senior medical students •Orientation for incoming medical students •Co-Advisor, Gold Humanism Honor Society •Co-Advisor, Alpha Omega Alpha •Medical Student Awards Committee •Graduation Committee •Summer Internship/Preceptorship Programs Minimum Qualifications: 1.M.D./D.O. or Ph.D. degree required 2.Recent higher education administrative experience working with students. 3.Knowledge of higher education and its practices and procedures. Preferred Qualifications: Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements for the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center will include drug and other required health screenings for the position. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to attracting and retaining the best and brightest talent and fostering a culture of respect. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact HR Compliance at hrcompliance@utoledo.edu or 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m. or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the Center for Administrative Support on the UToledo Main Campus. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 73533ee5 Last Name (required) d5a5982c Email (required) c21324f7 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. ED Registration Specialist H