    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/legal-assistant-hsc-health-science-campus-support-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states": {
      "title": "Legal Assistant, HSC",
      "description": "Legal Assistant, HSC - Health Science Campus Support Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Legal Assistant, HSC - Health Science Campus Support Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Legal Assistant, HSC 500878 Health Science Campus Support Toledo, OH Full-Time Legal None Staff - Full-Time Title: Legal Assistant, HSC Department Org: Office Of Legal Affairs - 104890 Employee Classification: U1 - Unclassified PSA FT Bargaining Unit: Professional Staff Association Shift: 1 Start Time: 8:15 End Time: 5:00 Job Description: This role directly supports the Sr. Associate General Counsel, Sr. Associate General Counsel- Healthcare, the Contract Compliance Officer, and the Legal Nurse Specialist performing a variety of duties such as preparing legal documents and correspondence, docketing cases, managing all legal files and providing information and direction to others. This position allows access to and deals with highly confidential information related to litigation, legal issues, strategies, and positions related to the University and its subsidiaries, including labor unions of The University of Toledo. Minimum Qualifications: • A minimum of an associate’s degree in legal studies is required or a combination of applicable experience and education in lieu of higher education. • Minimum of one year working in a law office/legal environment preferred. • Experience with healthcare and/or education law strongly preferred. Preferred Qualifications: • Must have exceptional interpersonal skills and the ability to foster positive working relationships across departments are essential. • Must be able to navigate complex interpersonal dynamics with tact and professionalism. • Must be able to solve problems and handle responsibilities under pressure. Ability to act independently, have good judgment and work with minimal supervision. Must be able to handle multiple tasks in an organized manner. Must be proactive in seeking out sources for instruction. • Must be familiar with a broad range of legal terminology. Knowledge of brief writing and citations. • Must have strong interpersonal and communication skills and the ability to work effectively with a wide range of constituencies in a diverse community. Ability to use diplomacy and discretion in giving out information and in referring and directing callers and visitors. • Must be able to manage confidential information and communications while maintaining confidentiality and discretion at all times. • Must have excellent computer skills, including Microsoft Word, Excel, Outlook, Adobe Pro, etc. • Preferred experience in legal management software. • Must have ability to create, compose and edit written materials. Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements for the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center will include drug and other required health screenings for the position. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to attracting and retaining the best and brightest talent and fostering a culture of respect. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact HR Compliance at hrcompliance@utoledo.edu or 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m. or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the Center for Administrative Support on the UToledo Main Campus. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 5dd158fb Last Name (required) 4c7fb32d Email (required) fc2d647d Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. ED Registration Specialist Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Registration - 108820 The ED Registration Specialist performs all outpatient and inpatient registrations functions, insurance verification, cash collections for the University of Toledo Medical Center while providing excellent customer satisfaction. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 2cddf757 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Full-Time Legal None Full-Time Legal None Employment Type Staff - Full-Time Staff - Full-Time Locations Health Science Campus Support Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Health Science Campus Support Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States First Name (required) 73e3cf0a Last Name (required) 5177e533 Email (required) c078ea82 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functi